cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ct-mask: first-order masking verification by two certificates"
message: "If you use this in academic work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: nickharris808
    website: "https://github.com/nickharris808"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nickharris808/ct-mask"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/nickh007/hw-verify"
abstract: >-
  Certifies each probe of a masked hardware gadget as independent of every secret, under glitch-free gate-value probing at first order with two shares. Adds a uniformity certificate alongside the usual dependence argument, which certifies gadgets a dependence-only analysis reports as leaky -- notably the output shares of a domain-oriented masked AND. Records mean-invariance and whole-distribution invariance separately, so a first-order verdict states its own scope.
keywords:
  - masking
  - side-channel
  - probing security
  - hardware security
  - formal verification
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-28"
